2057
01:22:58,830 --> 01:22:59,889
Garlic?

2058
01:23:00,500 --> 01:23:01,960
I don't think that's garlic.

2059
01:23:03,300 --> 01:23:04,630
(Giggling)

2060
01:23:05,269 --> 01:23:06,330
What's that?

2061
01:23:07,269 --> 01:23:08,540
- Deodeok? - It's deodeok?

2062
01:23:08,540 --> 01:23:10,670
(The cutting board is covered with deodeok.)

2063
01:23:10,870 --> 01:23:12,139
You're pounding on the deodeok?

2064
01:23:12,340 --> 01:23:14,439
- Yes. To make grilled deodeok. - The grilled deodeok is tasty.

2065
01:23:16,179 --> 01:23:17,649
Do you run a restaurant?

2066
01:23:17,950 --> 01:23:19,349
Do you run a side dish store?

2067
01:23:20,179 --> 01:23:21,750
Your side dish store would do well.

2068
01:23:21,750 --> 01:23:22,819
Right.

2069
01:23:23,849 --> 01:23:26,420
(Rolling on the deodeok to flatten it more)

2070
01:23:26,420 --> 01:23:28,160
This is relieving my stress.

2071
01:23:29,359 --> 01:23:31,359
No one born in 2000 would make grilled deodeok in their spare time.

2072
01:23:31,359 --> 01:23:32,729
Right. That's...

2073
01:23:32,859 --> 01:23:35,059
I've never seen this white precooked deodeok.

2074
01:23:37,000 --> 01:23:38,700
(Humming)

2075
01:23:40,899 --> 01:23:43,809
(She's joyfully pounding on it as if she's doing laundry.)

2076
01:23:45,139 --> 01:23:46,210
All done.

2077
01:23:47,109 --> 01:23:49,109
The girl born in 2000 is spreading out the deodeok.

2078
01:23:51,280 --> 01:23:52,280
(Coating)

2079
01:23:52,280 --> 01:23:53,479
- Gosh. - What are you coating them with?

2080
01:23:53,479 --> 01:23:56,420
For the first layer, I coat them with soy sauce.

2081
01:23:56,649 --> 01:23:57,990
I grill them first.

2082
01:23:57,990 --> 01:24:00,219
And then I coat them with a red sauce and grill them.

2083
01:24:00,519 --> 01:24:01,660
So you grill them two times?

2084
01:24:01,660 --> 01:24:03,189
- Right. - My goodness.

2085
01:24:05,160 --> 01:24:07,460
(Adding the sauces as if she has done it many times before)

2086
01:24:08,200 --> 01:24:09,759
(She makes the second-layer sauce in no time.)

2087
01:24:10,170 --> 01:24:11,569
(Cooking the soy-sauced-up deodeok)

2088
01:24:13,099 --> 01:24:14,939
- I see. You cook them first. - Yes.

2089
01:24:14,939 --> 01:24:16,300
- Is that a necessary step? - Yes.

2090
01:24:16,300 --> 01:24:17,469
- Right. - That way, it's tastier.

2091
01:24:19,040 --> 01:24:20,840
(Coating them with the red sauce)

2092
01:24:20,840 --> 01:24:22,580
This is amazing. How could she think to make this at home?

2093
01:24:22,580 --> 01:24:23,780
Totally.

2094
01:24:23,910 --> 01:24:25,509
(Flipping)

2095
01:24:26,109 --> 01:24:28,550
(She skillfully flips over the deodeok.)

2096
01:24:29,519 --> 01:24:31,219
(Shaking)

2097
01:24:32,990 --> 01:24:35,460
(She finishes the grilled deodeok with sesame seeds too.)

2098
01:24:36,189 --> 01:24:37,290
(Humming)

2099
01:24:38,729 --> 01:24:40,660
How can she cook so neatly? She didn't spill anything.

2100
01:24:41,030 --> 01:24:42,229
My gosh. Look.

2101
01:24:42,229 --> 01:24:43,729
- Goodness. - They look like store-bought.

2102
01:24:44,300 --> 01:24:45,729
(Stir-fried fishcakes, stir-fried potatoes,)

2103
01:24:45,729 --> 01:24:47,040
(chive kimchi, jangjorim, grilled deodeok)

2104
01:24:47,540 --> 01:24:51,410
(She will finish the side dishes instead of having delivery food.)

2105
01:24:53,069 --> 01:24:54,139
She doesn't eat delivery food.

2106
01:24:54,139 --> 01:24:55,410
Then she eats slowly.

2107
01:24:55,410 --> 01:24:56,609
She smiles at a stone.

2108
01:24:56,609 --> 01:24:57,979
- She'll live out her life well. - Yes.

2109
01:25:00,420 --> 01:25:02,019
(She grabs the wet wipe for the kitchen.)

2110
01:25:03,280 --> 01:25:07,389
(She starts cleaning right after cooking.)

2111
01:25:07,389 --> 01:25:08,859
Her induction range is that clean?

2112
01:25:08,859 --> 01:25:11,090
Look at the induction range shining even when she cooks a lot.

2113
01:25:11,090 --> 01:25:12,330
I see no oil stains either.

2114
01:25:12,929 --> 01:25:15,399
(She can't allow even a single stain.)

2115
01:25:16,229 --> 01:25:19,599
(She wipes the wall too.)

2116
01:25:20,340 --> 01:25:22,399
Nothing got on the white counter top.

2117
01:25:22,399 --> 01:25:23,399
No way.

2118
01:25:23,399 --> 01:25:25,639
It's not easy to maintain the white counter top that clean.

2119
01:25:27,380 --> 01:25:28,580
(Opening up)

2120
01:25:30,250 --> 01:25:31,910
(She grabs something rustling.)

2121
01:25:33,750 --> 01:25:36,019
- She's so frugal. - She's frugal.

2122
01:25:38,790 --> 01:25:40,420
(She reuses the plastic bags as the food waste bags.)

2123
01:25:40,420 --> 01:25:41,660
Gosh, she's amazing.

2124
01:25:42,460 --> 01:25:43,660
Out of all the people born in 2000...

2125
01:25:43,660 --> 01:25:44,929
I've never met anyone who manages her house better than her.

2126
01:25:44,929 --> 01:25:46,330
(Smiling)

2127
01:25:48,000 --> 01:25:49,599
(I cleaned everything to perfection.)

2128
01:25:51,429 --> 01:25:53,200
All right.

2129
01:25:54,269 --> 01:25:55,569
Gosh, she really knows her stuff.

2130
01:25:55,569 --> 01:25:57,370
She puts the plastic sheet over the container.

2131
01:25:57,370 --> 01:25:58,469
- Right. - To store them longer.

2132
01:25:58,469 --> 01:25:59,639
- Right. - That way, it doesn't smell.

2133
01:26:01,710 --> 01:26:04,280
(She puts the container in the fridge right away.)

2134
01:26:04,910 --> 01:26:06,950
(I won't have to worry about side dishes for a while.)

2135
01:26:09,080 --> 01:26:10,750
(Grabbing)

2136
01:26:11,849 --> 01:26:13,090
- The items you bought today? - Yes.

2137
01:26:14,059 --> 01:26:15,259
- The stone. - Take the stone out.

2138
01:26:15,259 --> 01:26:17,189
- You must take the stone out. - The stone feels stuffy inside.

2139
01:26:19,429 --> 01:26:20,729
(Laughing)

2140
01:26:21,000 --> 01:26:22,160
It's the stone.

2141
01:26:22,899 --> 01:26:25,170
It's in the plastic bag. It can't breathe then.

2142
01:26:27,170 --> 01:26:29,599
(She carefully takes out the rest of the items.)

2143
01:26:29,599 --> 01:26:30,840
I'm very happy with it.

2144
01:26:31,569 --> 01:26:32,609
(Raising)

2145
01:26:32,609 --> 01:26:33,740
What's that?

2146
01:26:33,740 --> 01:26:35,540
I told you about it. The zoomers take aerial shots.

2147
01:26:42,080 --> 01:26:43,689
- It will be in the diary. - Yes.

2148
01:26:43,689 --> 01:26:44,889
It will be in it later.

2149
01:26:44,889 --> 01:26:46,990
(She loves it.)

2150
01:26:47,620 --> 01:26:50,630
Even if I don't do anything special, it brings me joy.

2151
01:26:51,330 --> 01:26:52,530
Since I live alone,

2152
01:26:52,530 --> 01:26:55,399
I'm in the process of finding out about myself more.

2153
01:26:55,500 --> 01:26:59,269
I learned that I like plants, fish, and cooking food.

2154
01:26:59,269 --> 01:27:01,099
I clearly know what I like.

2155
01:27:01,269 --> 01:27:03,939
That brings up my self-esteem too.

2156
01:27:04,009 --> 01:27:07,939
It feels like I'm giving myself a joyful day every day.

2157
01:27:08,080 --> 01:27:09,679
That's how I feel most of the time.

2158
01:27:09,740 --> 01:27:13,580
I think I can treasure myself a little more.

2159
01:27:14,050 --> 01:27:16,019
I can do a good job.

2160
01:27:18,920 --> 01:27:20,920
(Placing her pet stone in the plant pot)

2161
01:27:20,920 --> 01:27:22,990
- I put it there. - That's so cute.

2162
01:27:23,830 --> 01:27:25,830
- That's cute. - Put it in the house.

2163
01:27:25,830 --> 01:27:27,099
What about its house?

2164
01:27:27,099 --> 01:27:30,030
Hold on. Those stones aren't your pet stones?

2165
01:27:30,200 --> 01:27:31,870
They don't come from a good family.

2166
01:27:33,670 --> 01:27:36,099
- She cherishes her everyday life. - Right.

2167
01:27:36,370 --> 01:27:37,639
She's amazing.

2168
01:27:37,769 --> 01:27:39,309
(Next story)

2169
01:27:39,710 --> 01:27:40,910
(CODE KUNST is shopping...)

2170
01:27:40,910 --> 01:27:42,139
(with someone.)

2171
01:27:42,410 --> 01:27:44,050
(It's his younger brother who looks just like him.)

2172
01:27:44,309 --> 01:27:45,580
(I prepared something for you.)

2173
01:27:45,580 --> 01:27:46,580
(Heart-pounding)

2174
01:27:47,679 --> 01:27:49,420
(For his brother who will get married soon,)

2175
01:27:49,719 --> 01:27:51,490
(he wants to buy his brother shoes for the wedding.)

2176
01:27:52,349 --> 01:27:53,719
(He already knows what his brother likes.)

2177
01:27:54,559 --> 01:27:55,790
(You're the best.)

2178
01:27:56,490 --> 01:27:57,859
(I don't want to go down the stairs.)

2179
01:27:58,729 --> 01:28:00,130
(He's the cool brother only for a moment.)

2180
01:28:00,130 --> 01:28:01,229
(He goes back to the playful brother.)

2181
01:28:01,500 --> 01:28:03,599
(Spending time together makes them nostalgic.)

2182
01:28:03,599 --> 01:28:04,729
(Nostalgic about their bets)

2183
01:28:05,370 --> 01:28:06,569
(You're making my blood hot now.)

2184
01:28:06,899 --> 01:28:09,240
(The dribbling is extraordinary for Sakuragi KUNST.)

2185
01:28:09,569 --> 01:28:11,340
(His brother is getting competitive too.)

2186
01:28:11,809 --> 01:28:12,809
(Eat your poop.)

2187
01:28:13,340 --> 01:28:16,210
(In the end, they play dirty like immature kids.)

2188
01:28:17,109 --> 01:28:18,550
(They become boys when they're together.)

2189
01:28:19,349 --> 01:28:22,849
(From Men to Boys with His Forever Best Friend)

2190
01:28:24,349 --> 01:28:26,750
(Jang Woo is standing in front of the frozen valley.)

2191
01:28:26,750 --> 01:28:27,759
(Sniffling)

2192
01:28:30,660 --> 01:28:31,660
(Grunting)

2193
01:28:32,729 --> 01:28:33,729
(Grunting)

2194
01:28:33,830 --> 01:28:34,830
(Grunting)

2195
01:28:35,000 --> 01:28:36,000
(It's been a long time.)

2196
01:28:36,300 --> 01:28:37,929
(To absorb the energy of Mother Nature,)

2197
01:28:38,030 --> 01:28:39,769
(I'm going camping.)

2198
01:28:40,500 --> 01:28:42,870
(Let's awaken my spirit in Mother Nature for the new year.)

2199
01:28:43,710 --> 01:28:44,840
(He decided to dive into the water.)

2200
01:28:44,840 --> 01:28:45,910
(Screaming)

2201
01:28:47,040 --> 01:28:48,679
(Spirit of the valley,)

2202
01:28:48,679 --> 01:28:50,179
(come to me.)

2203
01:28:50,340 --> 01:28:52,109
(Passed out)

2204
01:28:53,450 --> 01:28:54,950
(It's cold.)

2205
01:28:54,950 --> 01:28:55,950
(I'm hungry.)

2206
01:28:56,979 --> 01:28:58,420
(Just like a 1st-generation camper,)

2207
01:28:58,420 --> 01:29:00,090
(he uses three braziers.)

2208
01:29:00,559 --> 01:29:02,219
(Let me fill my stomach with good energy too.)

2209
01:29:03,090 --> 01:29:06,030
(Spirit of the New Year, Flame Up)
